{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":466,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counts binary words of length 12 avoiding 000 and 111.\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 identical bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. We can compute.\n\nLet A_n = sequences length n ending with single bit (i.e., last two bits different). B_n = sequences ending with double same bit (last two same, but third last different or none). Recurrence: For next bit, if we add bit same as last: if last run length 1 -> becomes run length 2; if last run length 2 -> cannot add same (would be 3). If add different bit: run length becomes 1 regardless of previous.\n\nThus:\nA_{n+1} = A_n + B_n  (adding different bit to any)\nB_{n+1} = A_n  (adding same bit to run length 1)\n\nBase n=1: sequences length1: \"0\",\"1\". For each, run length1. So A_1=2, B_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=12.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0 total=2\nn=2:\nA2 = A1+B1 =2+0=2\nB2 = A1 =2\ntotal=4\n\nn=3:\nA3 = A2+B2 =2+2=4\nB3 = A2 =2\ntotal=6\n\nn=4:\nA4 = A3+B3 =4+2=6\nB4 = A3 =4\ntotal=10\n\nn=5:\nA5 = A4+B4 =6+4=10\nB5 = A4 =6\ntotal=16\n\nn=6:\nA6 = A5+B5 =10+6=16\nB6 = A5 =10\ntotal=26\n\nn=7:\nA7 = A6+B6 =16+10=26\nB7 = A6 =16\ntotal=42\n\nn=8:\nA8 = A7+B7 =26+16=42\nB8 = A7 =26\ntotal=68\n\nn=9:\nA9 = A8+B8 =42+26=68\nB9 = A8 =42\ntotal=110\n\nn=10:\nA10 = A9+B9 =68+42=110\nB10 = A9 =68\ntotal=178\n\nn=11:\nA11 = A10+B10 =110+68=178\nB11 = A10 =110\ntotal=288\n\nn=12:\nA12 = A11+B11 =178+110=288\nB12 = A11 =178\ntotal=466\n\nThus answer 466. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790939315,"mode